 ## Overview
-Analytic-Splatting is a rendering method that replaces the point-sampling of 2D Gaussians in 3D Gaussian Splatting (3DGS) with an analytical approximation of the integral of the Gaussian signal over the pixel window area to reduce aliasing artifacts during zooming or resolution changes [S2]. Unlike [3D Gaussian Splatting Rendering (Software)](2805-3d-gaussian-splatting-rendering-software.md) which treats pixels as isolated points, or [Mip-Splatting](3410-3d-gaussian-splatting-mvp.md) which uses a hybrid filtering mechanism that suppresses high-frequency components, Analytic-Splatting preserves high-quality details by analytically integrating the signal using a conditioned logistic function approximation of the Gaussian CDF [S2].
+Analytic-Splatting is a rendering method that replaces the point-sampling of 2D Gaussians in 3D Gaussian Splatting (3DGS) with an analytical approximation of the integral of the Gaussian signal over the pixel window area to reduce aliasing artifacts during zooming or resolution changes [S2]. Unlike [3D Gaussian Splatting](2812-3d-gaussian-splatting.md) which treats pixels as isolated points, or [Mip-Splatting](3410-3d-gaussian-splatting-mvp.md) which uses a hybrid filtering mechanism that suppresses high-frequency components, Analytic-Splatting preserves high-quality details by analytically integrating the signal using a conditioned logistic function approximation of the Gaussian CDF [S2].
 
